# Valgrind suppressions for fun_test (Linux / valgrind 3.18+).
#
# Usage:
#   valgrind --leak-check=full --suppressions=../swinx/valgrind-linux.supp ./fun_test
#
# After the swinx-side fixes (hook.cpp use-after-free, SOUI RunIdle
# uninitialized MSG, test leaks), the remaining reports are all inside
# third-party libraries:
#
# 1. libxcb writev noise: the uninitialized bytes live in the 21,168-byte
#    connection block calloc'ed by xcb_connect_to_fd (X11 setup response
#    padding / outbound buffer reuse). swinx-side requests (e.g.
#    SendExposeEvent) are fully initialized.
# 2. cairo XCB glyph cache: 520 bytes definitely lost during
#    cairo_device_finish (SConnection destructor) - cairo teardown-order
#    artifact, not reachable from swinx code.

{
   libxcb-writev-uninit
   Memcheck:Param
   writev(vector[...])
   fun:__writev
   ...
   obj:*/libxcb.so.*
   ...
}

{
   cairo-xcb-glyph-cache-fini-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:calloc
   fun:_cairo_xcb_glyph_fini
   ...
}
